# --- this fork's build outputs -------------------------------------------------
# Appended, never replacing an upstream rule above. Upstream's own paths stay
# exactly as they were; these are the artefacts `zig build` and the
# `consumer/` package leave behind, which upstream's CMake build never creates.

# Zig's per-package build output and the manifest directory a fetched
# dependency materialises beside a build root.
/.zig-cache/
/zig-out/
/zig-pkg/

# The consumer package is its own `zig build`, so it has its own two.
/consumer/.zig-cache/
/consumer/zig-out/
/consumer/zig-pkg/